Package: flotestro-agent
Version: __VERSION__
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Architecture: __ARCH__
Maintainer: Flotestro <flotestro@localhost>
Depends: systemd, ca-certificates, passwd
Description: Flotestro fleet agent
 The agent connects a host to the Linux fleet management panel. It keeps an
 mTLS session to the control plane, reports the inventory and carries out
 only typed operations - the contract has no field for an arbitrary shell
 command.
 .
 Operations that require root are carried out by a separate helper process
 started by a systemd socket, which verifies the caller by SO_PEERCRED. The
 agent itself runs without root privileges.
 .
 The package installs the minimum: systemd, the trust store and the shadow
 tools the local account module changes accounts with. Every other module
 drives a tool the host already has, and a tool that is not there disables
 exactly one capability, which the agent reports as unavailable with the
 reason and the name of the missing package - it installs neither a network
 backend, nor a firewall, nor a backup tool, nor a journal forwarder of its
 own.
